    <string name="lesson_king_title">The King</string>
    <string name="lesson_king_body">The king moves one square in any direction. It is the most important piece: if it is attacked and cannot escape, the game is lost.</string>
    <string name="lesson_queen_title">The Queen</string>
    <string name="lesson_queen_body">The queen is the strongest piece. It moves any number of squares in a straight line or along a diagonal.</string>
    <string name="lesson_rook_title">The Rook</string>
    <string name="lesson_rook_body">The rook moves any number of squares horizontally or vertically. Rooks are strongest on open files.</string>
    <string name="lesson_bishop_title">The Bishop</string>
    <string name="lesson_bishop_body">The bishop moves diagonally any number of squares and always stays on squares of the same colour.</string>
    <string name="lesson_knight_title">The Knight</string>
    <string name="lesson_knight_body">The knight jumps in an L-shape: two squares one way and one square to the side. It is the only piece that can jump over others.</string>
    <string name="lesson_pawn_title">The Pawn</string>
    <string name="lesson_pawn_body">Pawns move forward one square (two on their first move) and capture diagonally. A pawn that reaches the last rank promotes to a queen, rook, bishop or knight.</string>
    <string name="lesson_castling_title">Castling</string>
    <string name="lesson_castling_body">Castling moves the king two squares towards a rook, and the rook jumps to the other side. Allowed only if neither piece has moved, the king is not in check and it does not pass through attacked squares.</string>
    <string name="lesson_enpassant_title">En passant</string>
    <string name="lesson_enpassant_body">If a pawn moves two squares and lands next to an enemy pawn, that pawn may capture it as if it had moved only one square — but only on the very next move.</string>
    <string name="lesson_checkmate_title">Check and checkmate</string>
    <string name="lesson_checkmate_body">Check means the king is attacked. Checkmate means it is attacked and has no escape: the game is over. Here, move the rook to the back rank to deliver mate.</string>
