    <string name="tip_day_1">Before every move, ask what your opponent wants to do. Half of all mistakes come from missing the opponent\'s threat.</string>
    <string name="tip_day_2">Look for checks, captures and threats — in that order. Strong players do this every move.</string>
    <string name="tip_day_3">In the opening: control the center, develop knights and bishops, and castle early.</string>
    <string name="tip_day_4">A knight on the rim is dim. Bring your pieces towards the center.</string>
    <string name="tip_day_5">Solve a few puzzles every day: tactics are learned by pattern recognition.</string>
    <string name="tip_day_6">After every game, review it. Your mistakes are your best teachers.</string>
    <string name="tip_day_7">In the endgame, the king is a strong piece — bring it into play!</string>
